<Shell title="Know your site before you go." direction="B / Site first">
  <section class="hero-visibility"><div class="frame"><span class="micro">Origin89 / The view from here</span><div class="visibility-heading"><h1>Know your site<br />before you go.</h1><div><p>Battery reserve. Solar production. Inside temperature. Bring the readings you check before a trip into one view, with control running at the site.</p><div class="actions"><a class="action" href="/next/sample-site/">Explore a sample site <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/next/equipment/">Find your equipment ↗</a></div></div></div><Console /></div></section>
  <section class="frame section-pad"><div class="section-title"><div><span class="micro">Made for the time between visits</span><h2>A clearer picture<br />of the place you care for.</h2></div><p>Origin89 is in development for remote and off-grid sites. Power is the starting point, with room for the pumps, tanks and sensors around it.</p></div><div class="journey-grid"><div><span class="micro">Before you leave</span><h3>Check the latest readings.</h3><p>See what the site last reported, when it was received and where a reading is missing.</p></div><div><span class="micro">While you’re away</span><h3>Keep the rules at the site.</h3><p>The Controller is designed to run configured rules locally. Remote viewing needs a working connection.</p></div><div><span class="micro">When something changes</span><h3>Understand the next step.</h3><p>Use equipment context and Buddy’s explanations to review what a change would mean.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="open-band"><div class="frame two-column"><div><span class="micro">Built around your equipment</span><h2>Mixed brands.<br />A shared view.</h2><p>Find your model in a research catalogue of {counts.entries.toLocaleString('en')} equipment entries. Each entry is a starting point for an exact-model integration discussion.</p><a class="text-action" href="/next/equipment/" style="margin-top:20px">Search the catalogue ↗</a></div><div class="reason-list"><div class="reason-row"><span class="micro">01</span><div><h3>From generation to water.</h3><p>Research spans power equipment, batteries, local I/O and passive devices. Catalogue presence does not establish shipped support.</p></div></div><div class="reason-row"><span class="micro">02</span><div><h3>Open through every layer.</h3><p>Hardware, firmware and apps are part of the open-source direction. See what is present and what still needs a public release.</p><a class="text-action" href="/next/open/">See the open stack ↗</a></div></div></div></div></section>
